credits-title = Credits
credits-paimon = Genshin Companion’s wish counter is a desktop remake of paimon.moe’s, by Made Baruna. Its banner and item data and its pity and rate-up rules come from the paimon.moe repository, used under the MIT License below. The item icons and banner art are downloaded from paimon.moe when first shown.
credits-genshin-db = The character archive (profiles, stats, talents, constellations) and the planner’s data (ascension and talent costs, farming days) come from genshin-db, by theBowja, used under the MIT License below.
credits-genshin-py = The HoYoLAB sync’s requests, their signing and the meaning of HoYoLAB’s error codes follow genshin.py, by thesadru and seriaati, used under the MIT License below.
credits-hoyoverse = Genshin Impact, its characters, weapons and banner art, and all other game content and materials are trademarks and copyrights of HoYoverse. Genshin Companion is a fan project, not affiliated with or endorsed by HoYoverse. It ships none of the game’s images: they are downloaded when first shown, and kept on this computer.
credits-amber = Character, weapon, material, element, talent and constellation icons and the wish art of the archive and the planner, downloaded from its copy of the game’s images when first shown.
credits-anime-game-data = The EXP needed per character and weapon level, from the game’s own data.
credits-wiki = The average drops of domains, bosses and ley lines behind the planner’s resin estimate, gathered by the Genshin Data Gathering team.
credits-uigf = Item ids from UIGF’s public dictionary, for exports other trackers read.
credits-font = Typeface by the Inter Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
credits-lucide = Icons by Lucide Icons and Contributors, under the ISC License.
credits-gpui-kit = The interface toolkit, under the Apache License 2.0.
credits-components = Genshin Companion is built with open-source Rust crates, each under its own licence, and embeds the Lucide icons and the Google Sans Flex font. Their notices and licence texts are here, and in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt next to the app in its download.
